Title      : gpu_poly: compare the left edge with drawingAreaRight as integers
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for PSX_MiSTer cd17b5a)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-10-31
Description:
  PREPARELINE skips a scanline when its left edge lies right of the drawing
  area: to_integer(xStart(43 downto 32)) > drawingAreaRight.  The left side
  is a signed integer, the right side an unsigned, so numeric_std's
  ">"(L : NATURAL; R : UNSIGNED) is chosen.  For a left edge < 0 (a polygon
  that starts left of x = 0, common for background polygons) the NATURAL
  argument is out of range: GHDL stops, Vivado synthesizes a compare that
  is TRUE, and the whole scanline is skipped.  In Crash Bandicoot 3 the
  background polygons on the left of the picture vanish in the frame buffer
  at x 0..511 and are drawn in the one at 512..1023: they flicker at the
  frame rate.  Comparing two integers gives the intended result.
  Checked with a Vivado funcsim netlist of gpu_poly against the RTL (xsim,
  random polygons with negative left edges, every output in every cycle):
  original netlist differs (fewer pixels, the left columns are missing),
  patched netlist identical.
--- a/rtl/gpu_poly.vhd	2026-10-31 13:15:36.392676541 +0100
+++ b/rtl/gpu_poly.vhd	2026-10-31 13:15:36.393710568 +0100
@@ -1013,7 +1013,7 @@
                      skip := '1';
                   end if;
                   
-                  if (to_integer(xStart(43 downto 32)) > drawingAreaRight) then
+                  if (to_integer(xStart(43 downto 32)) > to_integer(drawingAreaRight)) then
                      skip := '1';
                   end if;                  
                   
